Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:35:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 321/333] [ae-patch] Fix the Voice mode review findings: chat
 switch, mic handshake, muted finals, spoken answers

Review of the Voice mode patch found these, all fixed here.

Leaving a chat inside the 0.6 s grace no longer sends the new chat's draft: every timer, the pending card and the send wait are dropped when the chat changes. The mic handle now remembers a start that is still connecting, so stopping it cancels the start or drops the stream the moment it connects, and it reports every real change to Voice mode, including a failed start and the server's stream limit. A failed start is retried once after a second, then the speaker says "Mic unavailable" and Voice mode stays on; "Listening" shows only while the mic really listens.

Sound heard while the chat is busy, the voice is talking or the mic is returning is kept out of the draft. The send mute now follows the chat's own status (queued, running or streaming) instead of a five second timer, and a send the composer would refuse mutes nothing. A card that takes no answer of its own is never answered with the person's words.

Spoken answers are matched more strictly: a number counts only in a short answer made of number words, a label said after "not", "don't" or "never" is not picked, and "ok done" or "I'm done" end a multi-select card without leaving a stray answer. The browser switch is compared with the session's ae.voice label when a chat opens, and a failed label write is retried once. A tap on the speaker while it talks silences the rest of that reply until the next send, and the mic returns 0.3 s later.
